### The whole cross-module flow, in order. Run these top to bottom.
###
### Prerequisites:
###   docker compose up -d
###   dotnet run --project src/HelpDesk/HelpDesk.Api
###   dotnet run --project src/HelpDesk/HelpDesk.Notifications   (separate terminal)

@host = http://localhost:5199
@userId = 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111

### 1. Register a customer. Publishes CustomerRegistered.
# @name registerCustomer
POST {{host}}/api/customers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Rebel Alliance",
  "region": "Outer Rim"
}

### Capture the id from the response above.
@customerId = {{registerCustomer.response.body.customerId}}

### 2. Set prioritisation rules. Publishes CustomerPrioritiesChanged, which the
###    Incidents module handles to update its own replica.
POST {{host}}/api/customers/priorities
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "{{customerId}}",
  "priorities": { "Database": "Critical" }
}

### 3. Log an incident. Starts an event stream.
# @name logIncident
POST {{host}}/api/incidents
Content-Type: application/json
user-id: {{userId}}

{
  "customerId": "{{customerId}}",
  "contact": { "channel": "Email", "firstName": "Han", "lastName": "Solo" },
  "description": "Hyperdrive is making a noise"
}

###
@incidentId = {{logIncident.response.body.incidentId}}

### 4. Categorise it. Cascades TryAssignPriority, which finds the Critical rule
###    and asks for somebody to be paged over Rabbit MQ. Watch the Notifications
###    console.
POST {{host}}/api/incidents/{{incidentId}}/categorise
Content-Type: application/json
user-id: {{userId}}

{
  "category": "Database",
  "version": 1
}

### 5. Read it back. Priority is now Critical, assigned by another module.
GET {{host}}/api/incidents/{{incidentId}}

### 6. The same request again with a stale version. Expect 409 Conflict.
POST {{host}}/api/incidents/{{incidentId}}/categorise
Content-Type: application/json
user-id: {{userId}}

{
  "category": "Network",
  "version": 1
}

### 7. Closing before resolving is rejected. Expect 400.
POST {{host}}/api/incidents/{{incidentId}}/close
Content-Type: application/json
user-id: {{userId}}

{}

### 8. Resolve it.
POST {{host}}/api/incidents/{{incidentId}}/resolve
Content-Type: application/json
user-id: {{userId}}

{ "resolution": "Permanent" }

### 9. Close it. Publishes IncidentClosedForBilling.
POST {{host}}/api/incidents/{{incidentId}}/close
Content-Type: application/json
user-id: {{userId}}

{}

### 10. Billing lives in its own store and learned about all of it from one
###     integration event.
GET {{host}}/api/billing/customers/{{customerId}}

### 11. The full audit log, free.
GET {{host}}/api/incidents/{{incidentId}}/history

### 12. Marten writes the stored JSON straight to the response body.
GET {{host}}/api/incidents/{{incidentId}}/fast
